            <ArticleTitle>Cervical cord compression by the vertebral artery causing a severe cervical pain: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a cervical cord compression by the vertebral artery within the spinal canal is reported in a 47-year-old man. The clinical presentation, radiologic features, and the operative treatment are summarized. The mechanism by which this lesion caused a severe cervical pain is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
